        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Choose the bar first, then the holder.</strong> A screw clamp on
            a fixed, round front crossbar, with the screen near eye level and clear of the safety key,
            suits most treadmills, and the Arkon TAB131 is the simplest way to get there. Thick rails
            call for a strap, a folding machine for a quick release, and a walking pad for a desk
            mount.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Measure the bar and the device in its case before you order, keep the arm short for
            running, and take the tablet off before folding. For what to watch once it is up, see
            our guide to
            <a href="/how-to-make-treadmill-running-less-boring/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">less boring treadmill runs</a>.
          </p>
